    "note": "Text read is As Enrolled (05_EN), Am. S.B. 58, 135th G.A. R.C. 9.68 amended (underlined additions only: insurance and fee language, definition (6)); new R.C. 1349.84 to 1349.86 are the Second Amendment Financial Privacy Act (Section 3, uncodified, names it). Quoted 9.68(A) sentence joins existing text with the new underlined clause; nothing in it was struck. Also in the bill and not quoted: R.C. 1349.84 definitions, 1349.85(C)-(D) exceptions, 1349.86(A)-(B),(D) attorney general investigation, injunction and civil fine up to $1,000 per violation. Section 9.68's knife provisions are unchanged except the new fee ban covers knives."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 1 (R.C. 9.68(A)): Except as specifically provided by the United States Constitution, Ohio Constitution, state law, or federal law, a person, without further license, permission, restriction, delay, or process, including by any ordinance, rule, regulation, resolution, practice, or other action or any threat of citation, prosecution, or other legal process, may own, possess, purchase, acquire, transport, store, carry, sell, transfer, manufacture, or keep any firearm, part of a firearm, its components, and its ammunition, and any knife, without being required to have firearm liability insurance, and without being required to pay a fee for the possession of a firearm, part of a firearm, its components, its ammunition, or a knife.\nSection 1 (R.C. 9.68(C)(6)): \"Firearm liability insurance\" means a policy of liability insurance covering losses resulting from the use of a firearm owned by the person covered by the policy.\nSection 1 (new R.C. 1349.85(A)): Except for those records kept during the regular course of a criminal investigation and prosecution, or as otherwise required by law, no government entity or official, and no agent or employee of a governmental entity shall knowingly keep or cause to be kept any list, record, or registry of privately owned firearms or the owners of those firearms.\nSection 1 (new R.C. 1349.85(B)): No financial institution or agent of a financial institution shall do either of the following: (1) Require the assignment of a firearms code in a way that distinguishes a firearms retailer from other retailers; (2) Subject to divisions (C) and (D) of this section, decline a payment card transaction involving a firearms retailer based solely on the assignment of a firearms code.\nSection 1 (new R.C. 1349.86(C)): The attorney general has exclusive authority to enforce section 1349.85 of the Revised Code."
}